---
description: Resolve an amendment against an executed edition, trace scoped effects, and gate controlled migration.
args: { request: AmendmentReviewRequest; executed: ExecutedAgreementBundle }
returns: AmendmentProgramResult
uses: [amendmentEngine/frameBaseline, amendmentEngine/resolveOldSectionReference, amendmentEngine/classifyRetroactiveBilling, amendmentEngine/compareOverlappingAmendments, amendmentEngine/revalidateCutover, amendmentEngine/testExceptionPreservation, amendmentEngine/resolveTargets, amendmentEngine/resolveTemporalScope, amendmentEngine/applyOperationsToBaseline, amendmentEngine/walkAffectedDependencies, amendmentEngine/prepareMigrationRelease]
---
1. Bind saved = executed.checkpoint when present, otherwise null. Initialize scope = null, amended = null, impacts = null and release = null. Bind baseline = frameBaseline(request, executed.agreements), oldSections = resolveOldSectionReference(request, executed.executedEditions), retroactivity = classifyRetroactiveBilling(request, executed.billingHistory), and precedence = compareOverlappingAmendments(request, executed.overlapEvidence). Baseline identity must bind the exact executed edition to request.baselineHash; a draft or upload order is not execution evidence.
2. Bind targets = resolveTargets(baseline, request.amendmentIds, executed.executedEditions, oldSections) even when references are ambiguous. The returned map must retain every requested amendment as an exact target or an unresolved operation, rather than inventing a successful target. If baseline identity is unresolved, add that fact to targets.unresolvedOperations and do not compose any amended text.
3. If baseline identity is established and every requested target is mapped without ambiguity, bind scope = resolveTemporalScope(targets, request.effectiveDate, executed.evidencePages). Preserve explicit intervals, covered entities, exclusions and retroactive questions. Only when its coverage and precedence are resolved, and precedence.blockers is empty, bind amended = applyOperationsToBaseline(baseline, targets, scope, precedence, executed.evidencePages).
4. Initialize exceptionCheck as AmendmentGuardrail { disposition: "not-evaluated", affectedIds: [], preservedIds: [], blockers: ["Exception preservation awaits a resolved executed baseline, amendment target and temporal scope."], evidenceRefs: [], proposedActions: [] }. When amended exists, replace it with testExceptionPreservation(baseline, amended, executed.exceptionRegressions). Keep each lost-exception finding as a release blocker.
5. When amended exists, bind impacts = walkAffectedDependencies(amended, executed.evidencePages, executed.cutoverReceipts). Follow actual obligation edges to open tasks, approvals, notices and scheduled work. Completed historical acts keep their old scope. A reviewed linked correction is required for past billing; invoice history remains immutable.
6. Bind cutoverReview = revalidateCutover(request, executed.cutoverReceipts). When scope, amended and impacts exist, bind release = prepareMigrationRelease(request, baseline, targets, scope, amended, impacts, executed.exceptionRegressions, retroactivity, exceptionCheck, cutoverReview). This call returns a blocked release plan until all ambiguity, billing correction, exception preservation, cutover and exact reviewer/hash gates clear; it cannot claim migration execution.
7. Bind checkpoint = reconcileAmendmentCheckpoint(saved, request, executed, baseline, targets, scope, amended, impacts, exceptionCheck, cutoverReview, release). Return { caseId: request.caseId, baseline, targets, scope, composition: amended, impacts, release, guardrails: [oldSections, retroactivity, precedence, exceptionCheck, cutoverReview], checkpoint, commitAllowed: false } as AmendmentProgramResult. Null downstream fields identify work not yet executable; the checkpoint keeps the concrete unresolved targets and source editions for a later review.
